00:52:43,120 --> 00:52:45,680
It's easier to work in something that has no traction at the beginning.

685
00:52:46,000 --> 00:52:48,240
Not easy, but it's easier because you can imagine it.

686
00:52:49,040 --> 00:52:52,960
But coming down, it's like, yeah, it's easy to get sort of hopeless.

687
00:52:53,520 --> 00:52:57,920
Yeah, we were kind of hopeless, but kind of, let's do it.

688
00:52:58,080 --> 00:53:06,320
Like, let's use this time that we have off and improve the app, make, make the best travel planner better, like ever.

689
00:53:06,800 --> 00:53:12,320
And, uh, once everything comes up, people will have trips to plan their trips, you know?

690
00:53:13,600 --> 00:53:16,320
So, yeah, like we, we kept working on it.

691
00:53:16,800 --> 00:53:23,600
Um, we had some amazing supporters and work and subscribers that didn't cancel their subscription.

692
00:53:23,680 --> 00:53:24,720
So we, we, we did.

693
00:53:24,800 --> 00:53:31,120
We could maintain our costs of Tripsi and keep the business running and everything.

694
00:53:32,880 --> 00:53:36,960
At the same period, we incorporated the company in the US.

695
00:53:39,680 --> 00:53:45,840
I had a whole story to move Tripsi from my personal account at the Apple Store to Tripsi.

696
00:53:47,120 --> 00:53:48,960
It took like two years to do that.

697
00:53:49,520 --> 00:53:50,160
Oh my goodness.

698
00:53:50,880 --> 00:53:50,960
Yeah.

699
00:53:52,640 --> 00:53:54,960
But anyway, like, it all worked out.

700
00:53:56,400 --> 00:53:59,680
I think we did several updates in the app during the pandemic.

701
00:54:00,160 --> 00:54:00,240
Yeah.

702
00:54:00,960 --> 00:54:16,080
Even though like there there was no traction in March 2021, the app started getting traction again because people were traveling again after March 2021.

703
00:54:17,120 --> 00:54:24,880
So it was it was very slow but we could see that people were using the app.

704
00:54:26,320 --> 00:54:35,040
Just anecdotally, I remember, especially once vaccines started coming out, at least here in the States, there was like I forgot what they called it.

705
00:54:35,040 --> 00:54:45,040
There was a name for it, but it was almost like, uh, it was like vendetta traveling or something like people were they were angry and they had like saved up vacation funds or whatever.

706
00:54:45,600 --> 00:55:06,560
And so people were just like they just needed to go somewhere and they were traveling more than they would normally just to like do something, um, even if it was a drive to a more remote place or, you know, whatever, uh, it seemed like, yeah, around 2021 everybody's kind of like, all right, I just I have to literally have to get away from my hometown somehow.

707
00:55:07,200 --> 00:55:07,280
Yes.

708
00:55:07,600 --> 00:56:02,080
And and even like from the emotional perspective, people were stuck at home and locked down all the time like they they really wanted to go out and and talk to their friends and or visit their families outside you know so many people that need to travel to see their families or friends there's so many people that need to do that yeah so uh as soon as the borders are were opened and you could fly away you you you go like even if you had to use masks and do the vaccine and and do the not the vaccine the tests all the tests that you had to do to go on a plane, like I think was like honestly, I almost wonder if that would help something like Tripsi because traveling became way more of an intense organizational process, I feel like.

709
00:56:02,880 --> 00:56:03,920
Oh yeah, definitely.

710
00:56:04,480 --> 00:56:10,080
So many people were storing their tests, their tests and COVID and everything in Tripsi.

711
00:56:10,320 --> 00:56:11,440
Like it was very helpful.

712
00:56:11,600 --> 00:56:11,680
Yeah.

713
00:56:12,240 --> 00:56:15,440
Having a space to save that, don't need to print it.

714
00:56:16,080 --> 00:56:17,760
So Tripsi definitely helped that.

715
00:56:18,160 --> 00:56:26,960
I think we missed some opportunities to help even more in this case to give more COVID information to give more like information about airports.

716
00:56:27,200 --> 00:56:32,960
And it was all so confusing and so all overrandom the place.

717
00:56:34,400 --> 00:56:35,600
Yeah, all overwhelming.

718
00:56:36,480 --> 00:56:38,000
We could have done better in this case.

719
00:56:38,880 --> 00:56:44,560
So yeah, but anyway, like it's all probably gone now, I hope.

720
00:56:45,680 --> 00:56:45,760
Yeah.

721
00:56:46,640 --> 00:56:47,360
Fingers crossed.

722
00:56:48,000 --> 00:56:48,160
I hope.

723
00:56:48,400 --> 00:56:49,440
Yeah, fingers crossed.

