01:06:20,080 --> 01:06:20,800
Yeah, good question.

843
01:06:21,840 --> 01:06:32,960
So we look at the feature that we're implementing, we look at, is this going to cost us anything?

844
01:06:34,480 --> 01:06:35,200
This is the first question.

845
01:06:35,440 --> 01:06:37,680
Like, is this going to cost us anything extra?

846
01:06:38,240 --> 01:06:41,120
Like, parsing emails costs us money.

847
01:06:42,800 --> 01:06:44,240
Searching a flight costs us money.

848
01:06:44,720 --> 01:06:48,800
Like, storing a document on the cloud and having web access.

849
01:06:49,360 --> 01:06:50,160
also costs us money.

850
01:06:51,920 --> 01:06:59,280
So we need to balance this, like see how much money is it and how much of a unique feature is this one.

851
01:06:59,680 --> 01:07:20,240
Is this something that is very pro, is very like for the users that really are willing to pay to use and support or development, or this is something that maybe can drive the user to pay later, but they can keep using the app with this feature, you know?

852
01:07:21,040 --> 01:07:47,920
So I think each feature has each feature that you add in the app, you need to think through about all of these questions and think like, should I, like, should I charge the user for these or not, like in the next update that we are doing, we are adding weather kit, the weather kit integration.

853
01:07:48,640 --> 01:08:03,040
So weather costs money, like we have a free try, but it costs money and it's something that at some point., like, we'll probably be paying for it if we have enough users.

854
01:08:03,600 --> 01:08:05,200
So it is a pro feature.

855
01:08:06,240 --> 01:08:09,920
Time zones, we will also have these in our next, next update.

856
01:08:10,080 --> 01:08:10,800
Time zone changes.

857
01:08:11,360 --> 01:08:12,080
That's beautiful.

858
01:08:13,600 --> 01:08:14,960
It makes me very happy to hear.

859
01:08:15,680 --> 01:08:15,760
Yeah.

860
01:08:16,320 --> 01:08:16,400
Yeah.

